00:37:33.317 --> 00:37:36.721
welfare, aid for children,

00:37:36.721 --> 00:37:38.656
aid for battered children,

00:37:38.656 --> 00:37:40.157
all the things we do,

00:37:40.157 --> 00:37:42.059
the public hospitals system.

00:37:42.059 --> 00:37:46.197
New York City provides
universal healthcare

00:37:46.197 --> 00:37:49.000
through its public
hospital system.

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:51.636
Only place in America,
I think that does that,

00:37:51.636 --> 00:37:54.205 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we've been doing
it for 120 years.

00:37:54.205 --> 00:37:56.307
So our bills are very high.

00:37:56.307 --> 00:37:58.209
So, who pays those bills?

00:37:58.209 --> 00:38:01.979 align:start size:97% position:3%
Wall Street, all those
beautiful apartments you see

00:38:01.979 --> 00:38:05.316
on Park Avenue and 5th Avenue

00:38:07.385 --> 00:38:08.653
and on the West Side now.

00:38:09.587 --> 00:38:12.023
Every time a new area gentrified

00:38:13.190 --> 00:38:15.059
and the tax base
started to go up,

00:38:16.193 --> 00:38:18.062 align:start size:88% position:13%
I would see it as I
can do more for people.

00:38:20.398 --> 00:38:25.169
I can do more to make this
city a little more balanced,

00:38:25.169 --> 00:38:27.071
in terms of rich and poor

00:38:27.071 --> 00:38:28.939 align:start size:97% position:3%
and a little more opportunity
for people to move

00:38:28.939 --> 00:38:31.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
out of poverty, 'cause for
me, there's no question

00:38:31.942 --> 00:38:34.278
that capitalism is the
only way out of poverty.

00:38:36.981 --> 00:38:40.918
The rest of it is a false
program that's presented

00:38:40.918 --> 00:38:42.286
to people by condemn.

00:38:42.286 --> 00:38:45.189 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So what would you
do, like little things,

00:38:45.189 --> 00:38:48.993
like that now you can jump
