So you try to find, in
the prosecution field,

00:56:11.234 --> 00:56:15.772 align:start size:97% position:3%
you can find a lot of
apolitical people, good ones.

00:56:17.173 --> 00:56:20.744 align:start size:97% position:3%
So it said to me either
Mueller is losing something

00:56:22.212 --> 00:56:24.114 line:0%
or because the media let's
them get away with things

00:56:24.114 --> 00:56:25.715 line:0%
they don't let us get away with,

00:56:25.715 --> 00:56:27.217 line:0%
they're becoming very sloppy.

00:56:28.651 --> 00:56:32.789 line:0%
Because had a republican put
together that kind of a group

00:56:32.789 --> 00:56:35.291 line:0%
to investigate Hillary
Clinton or Joe Biden,

00:56:36.159 --> 00:56:38.595
there'd a been holy hell to pay.

00:56:38.595 --> 00:56:40.897 align:start size:84% position:16%
People who contributed
to the campaign,

00:56:40.897 --> 00:56:43.600 align:start size:97% position:3%
people who have made
statements that he was insane,

00:56:43.600 --> 00:56:45.568
people that made statements
that he had to be stopped

00:56:45.568 --> 00:56:47.170
under all circumstances.

00:56:47.170 --> 00:56:49.105
They shouldn't be on
a prosecution for.

00:56:50.540 --> 00:56:53.877
So I thought gee, Bob has
kinda lost it a little.

00:56:53.877 --> 00:56:57.714 align:start size:97% position:3%
Then when I came into the case
and I had my first meeting

00:56:57.714 --> 00:57:00.450
with him and he didn't
even know whether he

00:57:00.450 --> 00:57:04.988
could indict the President or
not, he had to go look it up,

00:57:06.156 --> 00:57:08.258
I said this guy's
really become lazy.

00:57:09.459 --> 00:57:12.462
Didn't realize that
he had an illness.

00:57:13.863 --> 00:57:16.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't realize that
the guy is suffering from

00:57:18.234 --> 00:57:21.070 align:start size:88% position:13%
some kind of a cognitive
brain impairment

00:57:21.070 --> 00:57:22.605
where he can't seem
to remember things

00:57:22.605 --> 00:57:23.773
or be on top of things.

00:57:24.674 --> 00:57:26.142
After that three hour meeting,

00:57:26.142 --> 00:57:27.977
that was the last
time we saw him.

00:57:27.977 --> 00:57:30.313 align:start size:84% position:16%
They kept him
under lock and key,

00:57:30.313 --> 00:57:32.715 align:start size:88% position:13%
kinda like what they're
doing with Biden.

00:57:32.715 --> 00:57:35.418
- That's exactly what
I was just gonna say.

00:57:35.418 --> 00:57:37.587
What about Trump
before all of this?

00:57:37.587 --> 00:57:40.523
'Cause obviously you guys
have become allies now

00:57:40.523 --> 00:57:42.158
and you spoke at the
convention of course

00:57:42.158 --> 00:57:44.727
and all that stuff, but
just from the pre-Trump,

00:57:44.727 --> 00:57:47.063
when he used to be
a media darling,

00:57:47.063 --> 00:57:50.433
when he was just a New
York City businessman,

00:57:50.433 --> 00:57:54.370
whether you liked him or
not, that's what he was.

00:57:54.370 --> 00:57:57.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you shocked at sort
of just the way everything

00:57:57.207 --> 00:57:58.341
is framed these days?

00:58:00.243 --> 00:58:02.178
- No, I'm not shocked,

00:58:02.178 --> 00:58:05.081
you know, I'd have to
go through a long story

00:58:05.081 --> 00:58:06.749
to tell you the whole evolution.

00:58:06.749 --> 00:58:10.353 align:start size:84% position:16%
I expected, unlike the
popular conception,

00:58:10.353 --> 00:58:12.422
that he would be
a good president.

00:58:12.422 --> 00:58:14.958 align:start size:97% position:3%
I also thought he would
probably get a lot of credit,

00:58:14.958 --> 00:58:18.561
more than he gets, because
he would defy expectations,

00:58:18.561 --> 00:58:20.430
kind of like Reagan did.

00:58:20.430 --> 00:58:23.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, they all thought
Reagan was a big dope.

00:58:23.666 --> 00:58:26.503 align:start size:97% position:3%
Reagan was one of the
presidents who probably was

00:58:26.503 --> 00:58:28.271
the best writer.

00:58:28.271 --> 00:58:31.674 align:start size:97% position:3%
I always tell people to go
read his love letters to Nancy

00:58:31.674 --> 00:58:34.143
and you find out what
a good writer he was.

00:58:35.545 --> 00:58:37.547 align:start size:97% position:3%
I used to help write speeches
for him and I was shocked

00:58:37.547 --> 00:58:39.816
at what a good writer he was
because I had the prejudice

00:58:39.816 --> 00:58:42.785
from the northeast that
he was just an actor.

00:58:42.785 --> 00:58:46.289
Well, I knew that Trump had
a very, very facile mind,

00:58:46.289 --> 00:58:48.892
very, very complex mind,

00:58:50.360 --> 00:58:54.697
had a very great interest in
politics and public affairs.

00:58:54.697 --> 00:58:57.967
You know, his interest in
trade goes back 30 years.

00:58:57.967 --> 00:59:02.906
His idea of our intervening
too much goes back 20 years.

00:59:04.641 --> 00:59:07.010
So these are things you
would talk to him about

00:59:07.010 --> 00:59:10.179
and because I was in politics,
the two things that I talked

00:59:10.179 --> 00:59:14.684
to him about most were golf,
golf, baseball and politics.

00:59:16.586 --> 00:59:20.056
We became friends
really because,

00:59:20.056 --> 00:59:24.227
when I ran in 1989, I was
gonna run against Ed Koch.

00:59:24.227 --> 00:59:25.461
He thought Ed Koch was

00:59:26.529 --> 00:59:28.031
had become a very bad mayor.

00:59:29.465 --> 00:59:32.368
He supported me in every one
of my political campaigns.

00:59:32.368 --> 00:59:35.505
We became good friends,
I joined his golf course.

00:59:35.505 --> 00:59:39.008
My son turns out to
be a fabulous golfer,

00:59:39.008 --> 00:59:40.643
professional for a while.

00:59:40.643 --> 00:59:43.513
He and the President
golf together a lot.

00:59:44.647 --> 00:59:46.449 align:start size:84% position:16%
They became very close
and Donald became

00:59:46.449 --> 00:59:48.017
like an uncle to Andrew.

00:59:49.152 --> 00:59:51.988 align:start size:88% position:13%
So it's through how
nice he's been to my son

00:59:51.988 --> 00:59:55.592
that I can see the
personal side of him

00:59:55.592 --> 00:59:58.261
and I also saw him
bring up his children

00:59:58.261 --> 00:59:59.963 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he's a remarkably
good father.

01:00:01.164 --> 01:00:04.000
So I see a side of him
that people don't see.

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:07.804
He was also always there
when we had police officers

01:00:07.804 --> 01:00:10.073 align:start size:84% position:16%
in trouble, fire
fighters in trouble.

01:00:10.073 --> 01:00:12.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
he and George Steinburner,
there's a whole group

01:00:12.308 --> 01:00:16.946 align:start size:88% position:13%
of New Yorkers that
somehow were painted as,

01:00:18.247 --> 01:00:20.049 align:start size:84% position:16%
maybe because they
were more conservative

01:00:20.049 --> 01:00:21.517
or they were more republican,

01:00:22.919 --> 01:00:24.621 align:start size:97% position:3%
they were painted as some
kind of ogres and they really

01:00:24.621 --> 01:00:27.223
were very, very kind
and very philanthropic.

01:00:28.124 --> 01:00:29.359
You can count on it.

01:00:29.359 --> 01:00:30.927
Finally, the thing
I liked about Trump

01:00:30.927 --> 01:00:32.395
is he wasn't a complainer.

01:00:33.529 --> 01:00:35.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
The mayor has to award
a lot of projects.

01:00:36.466 --> 01:00:38.768
I was scrupulous about it.

01:00:38.768 --> 01:00:42.071
Everybody supported me
in the real estate area.

01:00:42.071 --> 01:00:44.374
Anybody I gave it to,

01:00:44.374 --> 01:00:47.276 align:start size:97% position:3%
it could have been
considered a political favor.

01:00:47.276 --> 01:00:50.380 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I would set up committees
to make the decision.

01:00:50.380 --> 01:00:51.848 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would only reverse
them if they made

01:00:51.848 --> 01:00:55.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
a really stupid
decision, and invariably,

01:00:55.818 --> 01:00:57.120
my friends would be cut out

01:00:58.087 --> 01:01:00.390
and they come to
me and complain.

01:01:00.390 --> 01:01:02.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I would say to them,
didn't you support me

01:01:02.392 --> 01:01:05.361
because you wanted low crime?

01:01:05.361 --> 01:01:06.763
Yes.

01:01:06.763 --> 01:01:09.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said hasn't your
property value gone up 30%

01:01:09.499 --> 01:01:11.200
because the crime went down?

01:01:11.200 --> 01:01:12.135
Yes.

01:01:12.135 --> 01:01:13.302
Isn't that good enough?

01:01:14.170 --> 01:01:15.271
They would say no.

01:01:16.739 --> 01:01:18.374
We wanted that project.

01:01:18.374 --> 01:01:19.976
He never did that.

01:01:19.976 --> 01:01:22.745
I turned him down for the
biggest project that I had,

01:01:22.745 --> 01:01:25.715
which was the Time Warner
building because we thought

01:01:25.715 --> 01:01:28.284 align:start size:81% position:19%
somebody else's
design was better.

01:01:28.284 --> 01:01:30.787 align:start size:84% position:16%
He never once
complained about it.

01:01:30.787 --> 01:01:34.090 align:start size:97% position:3%
So this idea that he's always
looking for advantages,

01:01:34.090 --> 01:01:35.224
it's not true.

01:01:40.329 --> 01:01:44.200
He negotiates in a
way that looks like

01:01:44.200 --> 01:01:46.335
he's gonna squeeze out every,

01:01:47.737 --> 01:01:50.473 align:start position:0%
but then he's very, very careful
to stay within the rules.

01:01:50.473 --> 01:01:53.643
He always had very good
attorneys, the best.

01:01:53.643 --> 01:01:54.844
Very good accountants.

01:01:56.612 --> 01:02:00.016
I don't have an issue with,
everybody thinks oh my God,

01:02:00.016 --> 01:02:02.885
if they found his tax returns,
they're gonna find all this.

01:02:04.087 --> 01:02:07.356
I know every audit, I
know how it came out.

01:02:07.356 --> 01:02:09.125
They're gonna find nothing.

01:02:09.125 --> 01:02:11.160 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know what they will
find, is they'll find a lot

01:02:11.160 --> 01:02:15.431
of money, which you just can
just prejudice somebody with.

01:02:15.431 --> 01:02:16.899
Oh, look at all
the money he had.

01:02:17.900 --> 01:02:19.268
But they're not gonna find.

01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:23.906
- Right, having money isn't
illegal just yet, just yet.

01:02:25.308 --> 01:02:30.213
- They're gonna probably
find a group of tax returns

01:02:30.213 --> 01:02:32.415
that you can use in a tax course

01:02:32.415 --> 01:02:35.752 align:start position:0%
about how to do it right,
because that's what he paid for.

01:02:35.752 --> 01:02:37.720 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, well in many ways
it's usually that they're more

01:02:37.720 --> 01:02:40.089
pissed about the rules,

01:02:40.089 --> 01:02:41.624
rather than whether
someone broken them.

01:02:41.624 --> 01:02:45.361
That, we can usually agree on,
let's clean up the tax code.

01:02:45.361 --> 01:02:47.930
But that's a whole other thing.

01:02:47.930 --> 01:02:50.500
So, I got one more thing for
you that'll sort of segue way

01:02:50.500 --> 01:02:53.302
to the end here which is, I
mentioned at the beginning

01:02:53.302 --> 01:02:56.606
you did the episode of
Seinfeld with the yogurt,

01:02:56.606 --> 01:03:01.511
you did SNL where
you were in drag,

01:03:02.712 --> 01:03:04.714
those things seem so
distant culturally,

01:03:04.714 --> 01:03:06.482
from where we're
at now culturally.

01:03:06.482 --> 01:03:09.218 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like, SNL would
never put you on now.

01:03:09.218 --> 01:03:11.354
If there was a Seinfeld of now--

01:03:11.354 --> 01:03:12.855 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Because I'm a
republican, right.

01:03:12.855 --> 01:03:14.991
- Right, because you're a
republican and you know,

01:03:14.991 --> 01:03:17.894
if there was a hot sitcom now,
there really isn't anything,

01:03:17.894 --> 01:03:20.196
but if there was the
number one sitcom now,

01:03:20.196 --> 01:03:23.466
it would never paint
you as a nice guy,

01:03:23.466 --> 01:03:26.202
the way they painted you now.

01:03:26.202 --> 01:03:28.504 align:start position:0%
I just thought maybe this could
sort of take us to the end,

01:03:28.504 --> 01:03:31.507
which is as you've seen
the culture thing shift,

01:03:31.507 --> 01:03:34.110
as a guy that was on
the other side of it

01:03:34.110 --> 01:03:37.713 align:start size:88% position:13%
and now you're more
viewed as you know this,

01:03:37.713 --> 01:03:41.050 align:start position:0%
by mainstream let's say, is
like the scary Trump republican

01:03:41.050 --> 01:03:41.884
sort of thing,

01:03:43.252 --> 01:03:45.254
how is that for you personally?

01:03:45.254 --> 01:03:48.658
And then just also, as a
guy that's kept us calm

01:03:48.658 --> 01:03:50.426 align:start size:84% position:16%
through some pretty
terrible times,

01:03:51.427 --> 01:03:52.895
give me something hopeful,

01:03:52.895 --> 01:03:54.764 align:start size:97% position:3%
give the audience something
hopeful over these next

01:03:54.764 --> 01:03:57.767 align:start position:0%
couple of months, because I
sense people are really worried

01:03:57.767 --> 01:04:00.369
that things are gonna
get back to anything

01:04:00.369 --> 01:04:03.172
that looks like America from
literally four months ago.

01:04:05.074 --> 01:04:08.477 align:start size:88% position:13%
- First of all, I am
very down about the idea

01:04:08.477 --> 01:04:12.315 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we've been so
segmented and so stratified

01:04:12.315 --> 01:04:17.053
that even my...

01:04:17.053 --> 01:04:18.421
Warren Michaels is a
good friend of mine.

01:04:18.421 --> 01:04:20.690
I sit right behind him
at the Yankee games.

01:04:20.690 --> 01:04:22.959
I used to go on Saturday
Night Live all the time.

01:04:22.959 --> 01:04:24.293
I haven't been invited now,

01:04:26.062 --> 01:04:28.264
in 10 years.

01:04:28.264 --> 01:04:30.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I was pretty
good, I was pretty funny.

01:04:30.032 --> 01:04:33.736 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've actually hosted
an entire show.

01:04:33.736 --> 01:04:35.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
I have a secret
desire to be an actor,

01:04:35.938 --> 01:04:37.306
always wanted to be an actor,

01:04:37.306 --> 01:04:39.141
I guess that's why I
was a trial lawyer.

01:04:39.141 --> 01:04:43.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in Anger Management
and Out of Towners

01:04:44.814 --> 01:04:47.283 align:start size:84% position:16%
and a lot of the
Law and Order stuff.

01:04:48.784 --> 01:04:52.021 line:0%
I played the beast and
Beauty and the Beast.

01:04:53.189 --> 01:04:55.124 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
All kinds of roles, I
used to love doing that.

01:04:55.124 --> 01:04:56.626 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
I'm glad I got the
chance to do it

01:04:56.626 --> 01:04:58.928
because now you're right,
I would not have the chance

01:04:58.928 --> 01:05:00.363
to do it.

01:05:00.363 --> 01:05:02.298 align:start size:97% position:3%
Here's what I think is
hopeful, I think we're very,

01:05:02.298 --> 01:05:05.301
very lucky and I
really mean this,

01:05:05.301 --> 01:05:07.203 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're very, very lucky
to have a president

01:05:07.203 --> 01:05:08.704
with an indomitable spirit.

01:05:10.473 --> 01:05:13.109 align:start size:97% position:3%
Some other president,
given what he went through,

01:05:13.109 --> 01:05:14.510
could be broken by it.

01:05:14.510 --> 01:05:17.513 align:start position:0%
I mean, Nixon became an
alcoholic during the impeachment

01:05:17.513 --> 01:05:20.383
thing, or at least it's
rumored that he did.

01:05:20.383 --> 01:05:22.418 align:start size:84% position:16%
It could have
broken another man.

01:05:22.418 --> 01:05:25.187
We're very lucky that he
has an indomitable spirit

01:05:25.187 --> 01:05:27.290 align:start size:84% position:16%
because that'll
eventually prevail.

01:05:28.891 --> 01:05:31.627
Once we get past the pandemic,

01:05:31.627 --> 01:05:35.031
once this calms down and
it will, it always does,

01:05:35.031 --> 01:05:36.499 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's gonna get
back to the economy

01:05:36.499 --> 01:05:38.234 align:start size:84% position:16%
and how we're
functioning in jobs.

01:05:40.503 --> 01:05:42.204
He's gonna do miracles with it.

01:05:42.204 --> 01:05:45.975
I mean, he's got a remarkable
understanding of our economy.

01:05:45.975 --> 01:05:48.210
Some of the things that
he's been able to do

01:05:48.210 --> 01:05:50.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
really means that the
next recovery is gonna be

01:05:50.713 --> 01:05:52.848
faster and stronger
than the last one.

01:05:52.848 --> 01:05:57.453 align:start size:88% position:13%
Particularly, in boxing
out China so much.

01:05:58.554 --> 01:06:01.357 align:start size:84% position:16%
I see it as there'll
be a rebirth.

01:06:01.357 --> 01:06:04.760
The real question is,
if he gets reelected,

01:06:04.760 --> 01:06:06.062
which I think he will,

01:06:06.062 --> 01:06:09.632 align:start size:88% position:13%
and if he gets reelected
with a good spirit

01:06:09.632 --> 01:06:11.701
of the economy at
least coming back,

01:06:12.935 --> 01:06:16.339
will the democrats give
him at least two years

01:06:16.339 --> 01:06:18.140
before we go into
the next election?

01:06:19.342 --> 01:06:21.544
Somebody should get down
on their hands and knees

01:06:21.544 --> 01:06:24.280
and beg them to do that for
the good of the country.

01:06:25.748 --> 01:06:27.717
- Unfortunately, I think we
know the answer to that one.

01:06:27.717 --> 01:06:30.186
- Well, maybe.

01:06:30.186 --> 01:06:31.587
Maybe if they get defeated

01:06:33.189 --> 01:06:35.825
maybe they're gonna have
to reform their party.

01:06:35.825 --> 01:06:37.960 align:start size:88% position:13%
That's the only way
they're gonna get fixed.

01:06:37.960 --> 01:06:39.395 align:start size:84% position:16%
The only way they're
gonna get fixed

01:06:39.395 --> 01:06:41.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the way they got fixed
in the '80s or '90s,

01:06:41.797 --> 01:06:44.300
when they finally
nominated Clinton

01:06:44.300 --> 01:06:46.702 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he did the sister
soldier moment.

01:06:46.702 --> 01:06:49.338
They had been going
to far to the left,

01:06:49.338 --> 01:06:52.608
that we were trouncing them.

01:06:52.608 --> 01:06:56.579 align:start size:97% position:3%
Clinton, although maybe he was
more left than he indicated

01:06:56.579 --> 01:06:58.180
or certainly Hillary was,

01:06:58.180 --> 01:07:01.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
Clinton made a pretty
good show in '92

01:07:01.317 --> 01:07:03.285 align:start size:84% position:16%
that he was a
moderate candidate.

01:07:03.285 --> 01:07:07.456 align:start position:0%
And he was after all, a governor
of a conservative state.

01:07:07.456 --> 01:07:10.593 align:start size:84% position:16%
So he knew how to work
with conservatives.

01:07:10.593 --> 01:07:13.095
It was in his DNA to work

01:07:13.095 --> 01:07:16.899 align:start size:88% position:13%
with right wing senators
and assemblymen.

01:07:18.034 --> 01:07:19.502
He always knew how to do that.

01:07:19.502 --> 01:07:21.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I had a great
relationship with Clinton.

01:07:21.771 --> 01:07:26.175
I helped to pass the infamous
Prime Bill of 1994 with him

01:07:26.175 --> 01:07:28.177
and I have a great
letter explaining

01:07:28.177 --> 01:07:30.279
what a terrific mayor I am.

01:07:30.279 --> 01:07:32.915
I was gonna use that if I
ever ran against Hillary.

01:07:32.915 --> 01:07:33.749
(men laughing)

01:07:33.749 --> 01:07:35.484
- Yeah, for sure.

01:07:35.484 --> 01:07:36.786
Well listen, Mr. Mayor,

